# Fixture for tests/trace_label_test.rs.
#
# Four things, and each one is there for one label.
#
#  * `:B rdfs:subClassOf :C` with `:a a :B`. The rule table sees both, so
#    `rdfs9` derives `:a a :C` and a step claiming it is entailed.
#  * `:D` is absent on purpose, so a step concluding `:a a :D` is a bogus step
#    with every cited axiom inside the fragment.
#  * `:Adult rdfs:subClassOf [ owl:unionOf ( :Man :Woman ) ]`, the textbook
#    non-Horn axiom. tests/dlp_boundary_test.rs already establishes that
#    src/dlp.rs reports it outside the fragment, with the reason
#    "disjunction in the consequent".
#  * `:p1 :parent :p2`, which the supplied Horn table in supplied_rules.tsv
#    reads. Kept here rather than in a second file so both halves of the suite
#    label steps over one ontology.
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix :     <http://e/> .

:B a owl:Class .
:C a owl:Class .
:B rdfs:subClassOf :C .
:a a :B .

:Adult a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf [ owl:unionOf ( :Man :Woman ) ] .
:Man a owl:Class .
:Woman a owl:Class .
:s a :Adult .

:p1 :parent :p2 .
